From d4f5055b6f5ab5b7dd342849c685f1b87161f86a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:13:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] linker: Honour SDK_VERSION_OVERRIDES for text relocations
 again

lineage-24.0 changed the text relocation check to DL_ERROR_AFTER(23, ...),
which only looks at the process target SDK. The per-library value that
"linker: Apply TARGET_PROCESS_SDK_VERSION_OVERRIDE on library load" puts
in app_target_api_level was no longer used, so every blob with text
relocations was refused (gps.exynos4.vendor.so, libsecnativefeature.so,
libakm.so on i9100). Without the GNSS HAL, system_server blocked forever
in GnssNative.initializeHal and the watchdog restarted it in a loop.

Allow the relocations when the override sets an SDK below 23, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I940f12ded394f107092bc9fa8927dcef14ecb621
---
 linker/linker.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/linker/linker.cpp b/linker/linker.cpp
index 8964a38c3..0d31c1bdc 100644
--- a/linker/linker.cpp
+++ b/linker/linker.cpp
@@ -3487,6 +3487,12 @@ bool soinfo::link_image(const SymbolLookupList& lookup_list, soinfo* local_group
         break;
       }
     }
+    // DL_ERROR_AFTER() only checks the process target SDK, so honour the per-library
+    // override here before falling back to it.
+    if (app_target_api_level < 23) {
+      DL_WARN("\"%s\" has text relocations, allowed by SDK_VERSION_OVERRIDES (%d)",
+              get_realpath(), app_target_api_level);
+    } else
 #endif
     if (DL_ERROR_AFTER(23, "\"%s\" has text relocations", get_realpath())) {
       return false;
-- 
2.51.0

